## 3. Motion Logic [Certain]

- **What moves first:** nothing "enters" — the grid is present at t=0. There is no observable hierarchy of "background loads, then grid draws in." This is the biggest constraint on your rebuild: **you have no reference for hover-enter.**
- **What's continuous vs. discrete:**
  - Continuous/ambient: label-digit flicker (every frame, no easing), organic bloom growth (real footage, not something you animate).
  - Discrete/event-driven: the diagonal scan-pulse (cell-to-cell), the single blue accent flash.
- **How the scan-pulse builds and settles:** draw-in fast (~2 frames / ~0.15-0.2s to full opacity) → hold solid (~2 frames) → dissolve to dashed/faint (~2-3 frames) → gone. Total lifecycle per pulse ≈ 0.4-0.6s. Then it re-fires in an adjacent cell roughly 0.6-0.9s later. Two data points isn't enough to certify a fixed interval — [Guessing] on exact periodicity, but the *pattern* (travels cell-to-cell, doesn't repeat same cell twice in a row) is solid.
- **Hover enter/hold/exit — none of this exists in source.** Any interaction-state design for these is by definition `[Designed]`, covered in section 6.

