## 5. Interaction Analysis — Cursor-Localized Model [Mixed — marked per line]

Your instruction is explicit: the animation activates only in the region under the cursor; everything else stays idle. Source footage has zero cursor mechanics, so the *spatial* mechanics below are entirely `[Designed]`. The *content* that appears inside the revealed region (grid behavior, flicker, scan-pulse) is `[Certain, extracted]` — same rules as section 3/4, just now windowed through a mask instead of covering the whole plate.

- **Idle state** `[Certain, per your instruction]`: base Earth/nebula plate visible everywhere, no grid anywhere, no mask. Whether idle has ambient drift is open — see Q5.
- **Hover entry** `[Designed]`: the instant the cursor enters the surface's bounding box, a soft-edged mask fades/scales in at the entry point (~150-200ms), immediately followed by the local grid content appearing inside it (same per-cell stagger draw-in described in section 6, just clipped to the mask).
- **Active/hold** `[Designed spatial model, Certain content]`: mask follows cursor position continuously. Recommend an eased/lagged follow (lerp the mask's x/y toward the cursor's x/y each frame, factor ≈0.15-0.2) rather than a 1:1 snap — an instant-snap mask reads as a cutout, a slightly-lagged one reads as a physical lens. Whatever grid content falls inside the mask at any moment is what's visible; content is either (a) one pre-built full-surface HUD layer that the mask windows into as it moves, or (b) generated per-region on the fly. Recommend (a) — see section 7, it's cheaper and avoids popping.
- **Hover exit** `[Designed]`: mask shrinks/fades out (~200-250ms, faster than entry) at the last cursor position before leaving the bounding box — not a full reset to center, it collapses where the cursor actually exited.
- **Cursor influence** `[Designed]`: position drives mask location only, in the MVP. Do not tie grid content or scan-pulse timing to cursor speed unless you explicitly want that as a v2 embellishment — keeping it position-only is more predictable and cheaper to build correctly on the first pass.
- **Outside the mask** `[Certain, per your instruction]`: must never animate. No global grid, no full-surface pulse, no reaction to hover at all outside the masked radius.

